Test that the rounding scheme for `round of` money is the same in Z3 and OCaml.

```catala
declaration scope A:
    input x content money
    output o content integer

scope A:
    exception definition o under condition (x = round of -$$1.5)
        consequence equals 0
    exception definition o under condition (x = round of -$$1.1 and x = round of -$$0.5)
        consequence equals 1
    exception definition o under condition (x = round of -$$0.1
                                            and x = round of -$$0.0
                                            and x = round of $0.1)
        consequence equals 2
    exception definition o under condition (x = round of $0.5 and x = round of $1.1)
        consequence equals 3
    exception definition o under condition (x = round of $1.5)
        consequence equals 4

    definition o equals -1
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala Concolic --conc-optim=incremental -s A
┌─[RESULT]─ Concolic execution ─
│ Executed 6 tests:
│        Inputs │ Outputs
│ ───────── Test #1 ─────
│ x_in = $0.00  │ o = 2
│ ───────── Test #2 ─────
│ x_in = $0.02  │ o = -1
│ ───────── Test #3 ─────
│ x_in = $2.00  │ o = 4
│ ───────── Test #4 ─────
│ x_in = $1.00  │ o = 3
│ ───────── Test #5 ─────
│ x_in = -$1.00 │ o = 1
│ ───────── Test #6 ─────
│ x_in = -$2.00 │ o = 0
└─
```

